    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0189" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.00/344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. William C. Bullitt,
                        of the Division of Western European Affairs, to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-25">November 25,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Just as I concluded this
                        memorandum,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d83-f1"/> the appended telegrams were
                    handed to me.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d83-f2"/> They confirm my fears and
                    underscore my conclusions.</p>
                <p>I do not wish to be an alarmist but I feel that Bolshevism in North Germany is
                    inevitable unless we act at once and very wisely.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William C. Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d83-f1" n="7" xml:id="d83-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d83-f2" n="8" xml:id="d83-f2-content">
                <p>No indication on file copy as to which telegrams these were.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
